{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792865950,"nonce":"KDZoKan04/mRFbtpogSFZ5crDNo=","title":"TypeScript: interfaces with method signatures as types","message":"114 official rows stopped at interface method or index signatures; 39 of them at method signatures. An interface may now declare plain method signatures: it is a type whose property fields can be read, so annotated bindings, parameters and reads such as a variable used before assignment are checked as TypeScript checks them. Building a value of such an interface (from a literal, a class instance or another interface), calling or reading its methods, extending it and implementing it report Unsupported until methods have a native representation. Call, construct, index, optional and computed method signatures stay Unsupported.","files":null}]}